---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LineIcon from "../components/LineIcon.astro";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 1,
        "name": "Home",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 2,
        "name": "Services",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/services"
      }
    ]
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Power BI services | Alluvium"
  description="Power BI consulting offerings: Quickstart, strategy, project management, optimization, training, advisory, and migration, across finance, operations, sales, and more."
  canonicalPath="/services"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="service-fold service-hub">
<header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span>Services</span></nav>

<h1 class="page-title">Offerings</h1>

</div></header>
<section class="band band-alt"><div class="wrap">
<article class="card-feature card-quickstart">
<svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8"/><path d="M12 7.5v4.7l3.2 2"/></svg>
<h2>Power BI Quickstart</h2>
<p>Your most painful report, rebuilt in two weeks, with training and a week of support.</p>
<p class="see"><a class="btn" href="/power-bi-quickstart">See Power BI Quickstart</a></p>
</article>
<div class="cards-2">
<article class="card"><svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="5" cy="17" r="1.7"/><path d="M6.5 16.1 10.2 10.5"/><circle cx="11.2" cy="9.4" r="1.7"/><path d="M12.7 8.6 16.2 5.8"/><circle cx="18" cy="5.2" r="1.8"/><path d="M4.5 20.5h15"/></svg>
<h2>Analytics strategy roadmap</h2>
<p>A prioritized plan for your reporting: the decisions it must support, the data required, and what to build first. Your team knows exactly where to start and what can wait.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/analytics-ai-strategy-roadmap">See the analytics strategy roadmap</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round"><rect x="4.5" y="3.75" width="15" height="16.5" rx="1"/><path d="M8 9.2 9.3 10.5 12.1 7.7"/><path d="M13.2 9.2h3.8M8 13h8M8 16.4h6.4"/></svg>
<h2>Data and analytics project management</h2>
<p>Experienced, PMP-led management of scope, schedule, and rollout. You get a named owner, a stable scope, and reporting the business adopts.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/data-project-management-change-leadership">See data and analytics project management</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85"><rect x="3.8" y="3.8" width="7.2" height="7.2"/><rect x="13" y="3.8" width="7.2" height="7.2"/><rect x="3.8" y="13" width="7.2" height="7.2"/><rect x="13" y="13" width="7.2" height="7.2"/></svg>
<h2>Dashboard optimization</h2>
<p>A review of your existing Power BI for speed, usage, and conflicting numbers, followed by the fixes that make it faster and more trusted, so the meeting stops falling back to Excel.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/power-bi-dashboard-optimization-ai-insights">See dashboard optimization</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M7 6.4A7 7 0 1 0 18.2 12"/><path d="M18.2 12 20.4 8.8M18.2 12l-3.4-.4"/></svg>
<h2>Managed advisory retainer</h2>
<p>Ongoing expert support after launch to keep reports accurate, current, and consistent, without adding headcount.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/managed-advisory-retainer">See the managed advisory retainer</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="8.6" cy="8" r="2.4"/><path d="M4.2 18.7c.5-3.1 2.2-4.6 4.4-4.6s3.9 1.5 4.4 4.6"/><circle cx="16.2" cy="8.8" r="2"/><path d="M14 18.7c.3-2.2 1.6-3.4 3.1-3.4 1.6 0 2.8 1.2 3.1 3.4"/></svg>
<h2>Power BI training</h2>
<p>Hands-on training built around your own reports and data, not sample files. Your team learns to use them and adapt them as questions change.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/power-bi-training">See Power BI training</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 16.2h14M7 18.4h10M9 20.6h6"/><path d="M5.2 4.2h9.6v6.2L11.6 8.4H5.2z"/></svg>
<h2>Conversational analytics</h2>
<p>Ask questions of your Power BI or Fabric data in plain language and get answers grounded in your reporting.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/conversational-analytics">See conversational analytics</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><LineIcon name="connect" />
<h2>Power BI migration</h2>
<p>Move from legacy reporting tools to Power BI, rebuilt properly rather than copied file by file.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/power-bi-migration">See Power BI migration</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><LineIcon name="decision" />
<h2>Acquisition performance visibility</h2>
<p>Clear performance reporting after an acquisition: a gap analysis and a roadmap for the first 100 days.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/acquisition-performance-visibility">See acquisition performance visibility</a></p>
</article>
</div>
</div></section>
<section class="band band-domains" aria-labelledby="domains"><div class="wrap">
<h2 id="domains" class="section-title">Domains</h2>
<div class="cards-2">
<article class="card"><h2>Power BI for manufacturing</h2>
<p>See throughput and schedule clearly, with the shop floor and finance working from the same numbers.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/power-bi-for-manufacturing">See Power BI for manufacturing</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><h2>Power BI for finance</h2>
<p>Close faster, explain variance, and bring leadership P&amp;L and cash figures they can sign off on.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/power-bi-for-finance">See Power BI for finance</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><h2>Power BI for supply chain</h2>
<p>Track inventory, on-time delivery, and supplier performance alongside the financials.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/power-bi-for-supply-chain">See Power BI for supply chain</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><h2>Power BI for quality</h2>
<p>Put scrap, yield, and customer returns in front of leadership, not buried in a plant report.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/power-bi-for-quality">See Power BI for quality</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><h2>Power BI for HR</h2>
<p>Give HR headcount, labor, and people-cost reporting that ties to the P&amp;L.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/power-bi-for-hr">See Power BI for HR</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><h2>Power BI for sales</h2>
<p>Pipeline and bookings reporting that finance agrees with, so the forecast finally ties out.</p>
<p class="see card-cta"><a href="/power-bi-for-sales">See Power BI for sales</a></p>
</article>
</div>
</div></section>
<section class="band band-cta band-cta-accent" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <h2 id="cta-heading">Let's make your reporting work harder</h2>
    <p class="lede">Tell us what you need from your data. We'll help you find the clearest path forward.</p>
    <p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
